A||||7||AkursedX||Valvoline Maxlife Oil?||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||08-16-2001||08:15 PM||||Hi, I was wondering if any of you have any opinions on Valvoline Maxlife oil, good or bad.  I am planning on using this in my 87GT with 83k miles.  I would switch to synthetic, but there is alot of gunk in there and I don't want to loosen up all that stuff and cause plugs.  So I think that this stuff would be a pretty good alternative.<P>I have put this stuff in other people's car for oil changes and it definitly smells and looks different from conventional oils, but I'm wondering if it really does anything.<P>Any feedback is appreciated.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Kwez||08-16-2001||08:49 PM||||hehe, coincidences, coincidences !<P>I just bought a bottle (quart, pint?) of the stuff today !<P>I'm curious to know too.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Fformula88||08-16-2001||09:35 PM||||I haven't seen any good or bad criticism of it yet.  However, many of the oil additives that have come out have proven to be harmful to your engine.<P>How about some opinions with putting the synthetic in the engine.  I haven't had any bad experiences going to synthetics with Fiero's (went to Mibil one 69K on the 85 SE, 72K on the Formula.)<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kwez||08-23-2001||01:22 PM||||hmmm, ok, I didn't know about that (additives).<P>I thought that synth wasn't recommended for older engines ?<BR>obviously it depends on the condition of the engine.<P>Maybe I'll just stick to the good ol' normal stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||01:28 PM||||I dont think I would ever use sythetic oil again last year di an oil change with the stuff on my wifes 88 560 sel that has 160.000 miles on and it caused the valve guide seals to self destruct after about 15 miles of driving.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||08-23-2001||01:50 PM||||I've used Valvoline Maxlife in the last 3 or 4 oil changes I've done and I've been happy with it and I do a ton of driving.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-23-2001||07:42 PM||||Synthetic oil killed the valve seals.... plllease... If anything it washed crap out of the valve guides and the already trashed seals.<P>I put Mobil 1 in my 4 cyl at over 150,000 miles. The engine runs  better and if anything uses less oil than it did on crude base. The Mobil one is over due for change and still not nearly as filthy as any crude at 3000 miles.<P>There are several items along the same vein as Max Life. The main idea is to add conditioners that soften,swell, and/or prevent hardening of seals. <A HREF="http://www.barsleaks.com/" TARGET=_blank>Bars brand</A> makes engine and transmission stop leak products that are on this line... These types of additives are not likely to hurt a motor. Now will they do anything good? it depends just what condition the engine is in. No additve will help a motor on the way out, but they can help with seals that are starting to get blah and making little leaks.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AkursedX||08-23-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Synthetic oil killed the valve seals.... plllease... If anything it washed crap out of the valve guides and the already trashed seals.<BR>.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I was thinking the same thing myself.  But, this is the exact reason why I am wary about switching to a synthetic base.  <P>The engine only has 83k on it, but it still looks pretty dirty underneath the oil cap.  My 88GT which was babied and always ran on synthetic oil was crystal clear underneath the oil cap and it has 13k more miles on it.  <P>And like I said before, I have put this oil in other people's vechicles, and it looks and smells NOTHING like a regular oil (It has a very red color and it smells TERRIBLE!!)  So what I'm hoping is that it'll clean up the engine somewhat and condition the valve seals as well so I don't have any leaks.    <BR>||||reg||1
